          "blocks": {
            "reason_1": {
              "type": "_expanding-panel",
              "settings": {
                "number": "01",
                "label": "Inflation protection",
                "title": "Money can be printed. Gold can't.",
                "text": "<p>Governments can create as much money as they want, and every new bill makes the ones you already have worth a little less. Gold is limited, and getting more out of the ground is slow and expensive. Savings kept in gold can't be watered down.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "reason_2": {
              "type": "_expanding-panel",
              "settings": {
                "number": "02",
                "label": "Crisis resilience",
                "title": "It holds up when everything else falls.",
                "text": "<p>Stocks, property and most investments depend on the same economy, so they tend to rise and fall together. Gold moves on its own, and it often gets stronger when people are worried. It works hardest exactly when the rest of your savings need support.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "reason_3": {
              "type": "_expanding-panel",
              "settings": {
                "number": "03",
                "label": "Independence",
                "title": "It isn't anyone's promise.",
                "text": "<p>A bank account, a bond or a share is a promise from a bank, a government or a company. If they can't keep it, you lose with them. Gold doesn't depend on anyone: its value is in the metal itself.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "reason_4": {
              "type": "_expanding-panel",
              "settings": {
                "number": "04",
                "label": "Institutional conviction",
                "title": "The people who print money buy gold.",
                "text": "<p>Central banks, the institutions that issue the world's currencies, are some of gold's biggest buyers. They know the limits of money better than anyone. Owning gold puts you on the same side as the best-informed players in the world economy.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "reason_5": {
              "type": "_expanding-panel",
              "settings": {
                "number": "05",
                "label": "Global liquidity",
                "title": "Valued everywhere, easy to sell.",
                "text": "<p>Gold is recognized in every country and every language, no matter the border or the government. That means it can be turned into cash almost anywhere in the world. Few assets protect your money and stay this flexible at the same time.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "reason_1",
            "reason_2",
